> Come, let us finish this performance we've all been waiting for. Together.
> — Phrolova
 She is a particularly powerful Resonator and a former Overseer of the [[Fractsidus]]. Her forte can manipulate and transfigure the frequencies of humans, Echoes, and Tacet Discords alike. 

A life filled with unexpected suffering, grief, and betrayal led this former musician to align with the Fractsidus, in which she seeks to rekindle a past from which she was the sole survivor. After working with the Fractsidus for a long time, she made a promise with the leader, the [[Grand Architect]] to complete one final task. Following its completion in {{Quest|Dawn Breaks on Dark Tides}}, she left the organization to find her own path.

After completing {{Quest|Dreamcatchers in the Secret Gardens}}, she can be found in the [[Lost Beyond]].

==Official Introduction==
Phrolova, a Fractsidus Overseer walking the fine line between life and death, an uncanny, deadly conductor.

A silent wave of her baton is enough to attune the very frequencies of being and conduct the symphonies of "souls." The music of hers can sculpt a better world or, just as easily, summon a legion to wreak havoc.> The silent and somber Overseer of the Fractsidus, Phrolova carries an endless sadness that envelops everyone around her.
She weaves music that bridges the gap between life and death, crafting an ideal world within her heart.
> — [https://wutheringwaves.kurogames.com/en/main#resonators Introduction from the Official Website.]

==Trivia== 
* Phrolova has recurring thematical ties to death and the underworld.
** The Lycoris radiata or red spider lily is a flower that symbolizes death and the afterlife, especially in Japan and China.
** [[Hecate]], the Tacet Discord she summons and her closest companion, is described as a three-faced Witch of the Underworld from a [[Sonoro Sphere]] where all decaying frequencies converge, known as the "Beyond" or "Lost Beyond". Hecate is a goddess from Greek mythology associated with magic, witchcraft, and fittingly, with crossroads, similar to Phrolova's association with the [[Lost Beyond]].
* As of Chapter II's climax, Phrolova was implied to represent the true identity of [[The Shepherd]], since she was known to manipulate Echoes and Tacet Discords alike, and possibly sacrificing anyone to become Tacet Discords.

===Etymology===
* "Phrolova" is a stylized spelling of "Frolova" (Фролова), a common Russian surname (the feminine form of Frolov). The use of the Greek digraph "Ph" instead of "F" is an aesthetic choice by the developers.
* The surname is derived from the Russian given name "Frol" (Фрол), which is a colloquial form of the ancient baptismal name "Flor" (Флор). This name originates from the Latin word ''florus'', meaning "blooming", "flowering", or "bright" (from ''flos'', meaning flower).
* The suffix "-ova" is a Russian possessive ending, historically meaning "belonging to" or "daughter/wife of Frolov."